NUM-49: do not apply a removal that was never computed (R = -1)

treatmnt_treat() sets every removal to -1 ("not computed") and the apply pass
only skipped R[p] == 0. Once a cyclic treatment latches ErrCode, getRemoval()
returns 0 for every pollutant evaluated after it without assigning R[p], so
the apply pass used R = -1: a concentration-type equation then set the node
concentration to 2*C and the created mass never reached the mass balance.
Skip any R[p] <= 0, as 6.0.0 already does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-49_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/treatmnt.c b/src/legacy/engine/treatmnt.c
index 3638cd3..1bc0f49 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/treatmnt.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/treatmnt.c
@@ -234,7 +234,8 @@ void  treatmnt_treat(int j, double q, double v, double tStep)
     // --- update nodal concentrations and mass balances
     else for ( p = 0; p < Nobjects[POLLUT]; p++ )
     {
-        if ( R[p] == 0.0 ) continue;
+        // --- skip R[p] = -1 too (removal never computed)
+        if ( R[p] <= 0.0 ) continue;
         treatment = &Node[j].treatment[p];
 
         // --- removal-type treatment equations get applied to inflow stream
